{
  "_about": [
    "The room's movable axes. Each row has two halves:",
    "",
    "  SCENE (left)   id, label, unit, min, max, speed, default",
    "                 what the 3D room and setups use. Keep the ids: setups and ACQUA refer to them.",
    "  WIRING (right) device, ch, verified, note",
    "                 which Pi and which firmware axis really drive it. FILL THIS IN on the rig.",
    "",
    "Until a row has \"verified\": true it NEVER moves for real: the 3D room and simulation can",
    "use it, a real setup that includes it is refused (503) before anything moves.",
    "The device / ch below are only the plan (the same as ACQUA's acqua/crane.py), not checked.",
    "",
    "Filling in one axis on the rig:",
    "  1. device   the Pi's Device ID in the control center (pi-01 ... pi-07), or null if not wired",
    "  2. ch       the firmware axis on that Pi's Arduino: SX / SY / SZ (rails), R (turntable), T (tilt)",
    "              (Devices page: send <ch>H and watch which motor homes)",
    "  3. min/max  the travel in room metres (or degrees). For rails, firmware 0 mm = the home switch",
    "              = min, so max = min + (calibrated travel in mm) / 1000",
    "  4. verified true, once the steps above were checked on the real rig",
    "  5. note     anything worth remembering (motor, Arduino pin, quirks); free text",
    "",
    "ORDER MATTERS: a setup moves its axes one at a time, in the order of this list,",
    "so put axes that must clear the way first.",
    "",
    "To edit without rebuilding the image, copy this file to data/room.json and edit that copy:",
    "data/room.json wins when it exists and is reloaded on save (a broken edit keeps the old table",
    "and the 3D room shows the error).",
    "",
    "Other fields: unit m (sent as mm from min) or deg (sent as is); speed in units per second, only",
    "for time estimates and the 3D animation; default = where the 3D room draws an axis whose position",
    "is not known yet."
  ],
